description:
Make every event-appending mutation capture the event log as its bounded end, so no mutation reads the log's records.

## Background

The append base of an event-appending mutation is the log's length and final line (`CaptureSpec::discover_tail`, `crates/jit/src/repository_state/image.rs`). Several captures still request `VirtualPath::EVENTS` whole, reading the full log on every run:

- `publish_captured_issue_mutation` (`commands/mod.rs`), shared by issue lifecycle and field mutations;
- document add, remove and asset rescan (`commands/document.rs`);
- gate evaluation (`capture_gate_evaluation_image`, `commands/gate_check.rs`);
- gate preset apply and gate registry mutations (`commands/gate.rs`);
- template apply (`commands/template.rs`);
- profile apply and refresh (`commands/profile.rs`);
- init and re-initialization over an existing data root (`commands/init.rs`, `repository_state/initialize.rs`, read again by `events_action`, which errors on a tail).

Profile and init reach `capture_proposed_base` with the log among their extra paths (`scaffold.delta_paths()` in `commands/init.rs`, `events_path` in `commands/profile.rs`), and a whole request wins over the base's tail in `discover_tail`, so those extra paths must change too. Their `validate_repository` calls read no event log.

A profile's composition reads only the log's final line (`captured_log_end`), so the torn-tail marker does not hold this back.

## Success Criteria

- [hard] REQ-01: Each listed capture requests the event log through `discover_tail`, and re-initialization decides whether the log exists from the tail entry.
- [hard] REQ-02: A test shows that a mutation from each listed command family succeeds when every line of the event log except the final one is unparseable.
